From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PixelOS PIF <pif@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] key attestation: remove manual patch-level overrides

Use the existing Build.VERSION.SECURITY_PATCH defaults for attestation
instead of a free-text Secure setting. Remove the configuration parser,
refresh state, setting constant and validator. Old stored values no longer
affect certificate generation after the developer preference is removed.

---
diff --git a/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java b/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java
--- a/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java
+++ b/core/java/android/provider/Settings.java
@@ -13987,16 +13987,6 @@
         public static final String TRICKY_STORE_TARGET = "tricky_store_target";

         /**
-         * Optional patch levels used in generated attestations, in
-         * {@code system=YYYY-MM-DD}, {@code vendor=...}, {@code boot=...} or
-         * {@code all=...} form, one per line. An unset or empty value uses the
-         * running build's security patch level.
-         * @hide
-         */
-        @Readable
-        public static final String TRICKY_STORE_PATCH = "tricky_store_patch";
-
-        /**
          * Network traffic indicator mode
          * 0 = Don't show network traffic indicator
          * 1 = Display up-stream traffic only
